  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Warmer and more humid conditions promote \nincreasing odds for rain through Thursday \n\nSfc dewpoints are up +15 to +25 degrees since early Tuesday\nmorning, marking the return to warmer and more humid sensible \nweather conditions across CPA. Ongoing heating/destabilization\nof very muggy, high dewpoint air (Td 65-70F) across west- \ncentral PA will lead to moderate CAPE values by mid afternoon. \nWidely scattered thunderstorm development is expected, in a \nregime of relatively weak westerly flow aloft and poor mid \nlevel lapse rates. PWAT values approaching 2 inches could favor \na few locally heavy downpours. Continued low level WAA and \nslowly declining MUCAPE suggest scattered showers and storms \ncould persist overnight into early Thursday morning with HREF \nPMM signal focusing max POPs over the western Alleghenies. \n\nA subtropical high aloft will persist over the southern Plains \nand lower MS Valley through tomorrow. Around the periphery of \nthe high and in response to a shortwave trough crossing ON/QC, a\nsurface cold front will move slowly south/southeastward from the\nlower Great Lakes across Pennsylvania and adjacent states. This\nbaroclinic/frontal zone will provide a trigger for showers and a\nfew thunderstorm clusters through Thursday evening. The threat \nfor severe storms is low enough that SPC has not introduced \nprobabilities with the D2 update. WPC will maintain a level 1\nexcessive rain risk over the west-cetentral Alleghenies given \nhigh pwats and above normal rainfall over the past 7-10 days. \nWhile it's very likely that most of central PA picks up some\nrainfall by Thursday night, we do not anticipate a washout. \n\nAnother taste of Fall is on the way for the end of the week with\nnoticeably cooler and much drier/less humid air poised to return\nbehind the front (Td crashing into the 40s/50s). Expect a crisp\nand cool overnight Friday/Saturday morning with some upper 30s\npossible across the northern tier. Dry/fair wx conditions are \nforecast to start the weekend and last through the day on\nSaturday followed by periods of rain Saturday night through\nearly next week.",
